  year={2026},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-3},
  abstract={This work presents a dual-zero-compensation ring amplifier, which introduces two left-half-plane (LHF) real zeros to enhance the phase margin. In doing so, the proposed architecture achieves both high open loop gain and stable operation. Integrated into a two-stage pipelined-SAR ADC, the amplifier enables an SNDR of 60.8 dB at a sampling rate of 2.5 GS/s with Nqyuist rate input. This corresponds to a FoMs of 168.9 dB and a FoMw of $8.7 \text{fJ} /$ conversion-step.},
  keywords={Poles and zeros;Amplifiers;Printing;Technology;Gain;Timing;Frequency;Displays;Indexes;Indexing;Analog-to-digital converter (ADC);zeros and poles;Zero-point compensation;SAR-assisted pipeline ADC;Time interleaving SAR ADC},
